## 6. Kernel, Dracut, & Bootloader Setup
Set up Package Flags for the Distribution Kernel installation hook:
```bash
mkdir -p /etc/portage/package.use
echo "sys-kernel/installkernel dracut -uki -systemd" > /etc/portage/package.use/installkernel
echo "sys-apps/systemd-utils boot kernel-install" >> /etc/portage/package.use/systemd-utils

mkdir -p /etc/portage/package.accept_keywords
echo "sys-kernel/installkernel" >> /etc/portage/package.accept_keywords/installkernel
```

Build your primary system utilities layout:
```bash
emerge --oneshot sys-apps/systemd-utils sys-kernel/installkernel sys-fs/btrfs-progs sys-fs/cryptsetup
```

### Configure Dracut for Encrypted Btrfs & Clevis TPM2 Binding
```bash
nano /etc/dracut.conf.d/storage.conf
```
Add these required flags so Dracut packs the LUKS, Btrfs, and the Clevis decryption hooks directly into the initramfs image:
```ini
hostonly="no"
add_dracutmodules+=" crypt btrfs dm clevis "
add_drivers+=" dm_crypt encrypted nvme ahci btrfs tpm_tis tpm_crb "
force_drivers+=" dm_crypt btrfs tpm_tis tpm_crb "
```

### Install the Distribution Kernel
```bash
emerge --ask sys-kernel/gentoo-kernel
```

### Install Limine to NVRAM & Setup Configuration
Deploy Limine's bootloader binaries directly onto your unencrypted partition boot path:
```bash
limine install
```

Find your specific partition UUID parameters by running `blkid`. Use those real strings inside your brand new `limine.conf`:
```bash
nano /boot/limine.conf
```
Paste the completed corrected layout structure:
```ini
timeout: 3

/Gentoo Linux
    protocol: linux
    kernel_path: boot():/vmlinuz-7.3.1-gentoo-dist
    module_path: boot():/initramfs-7.3.1-gentoo-dist.img
    cmdline: rd.luks.uuid=YOUR_NVME0N1P2_LUKS_UUID_HERE root=UUID=YOUR_BTRFS_SUBVOL_ROOT_UUID_HERE rootfstype=btrfs rootflags=subvol=@ lsm=landlock,lockdown,yama,integrity,apparmor,bpf rw
```

