## 7. Clevis TPM2 Security Binding
Once your kernel and initramfs are generated with the proper drivers, bind your unmapped LUKS container (`/dev/nvme0n1p2`) to your secure hardware TPM2 chip using PCR states `1` and `7` (Firmware configuration and Secure Boot state). 

```bash
# Verify your TPM2 chip is active and accessible
tpm2_pcrread sha256:1,7

# Bind the LUKS2 container to the local TPM2 module via Clevis
clevis luks bind -d /dev/nvme0n1p2 tpm2 '{"pcr_ids":"1,7"}'

# Enable clevis parsing hooks inside OpenRC environment
rc-update add clevis boot
```

